, discarding it increases chance for All Simples.  \n2. Only 1 J2 remains, making Dragon Pung unlikely.  \n3. Keeping simple tiles (W5, W8, T2, T4) offers more flexibility for sequences or pairs.  \n\nReason:  \nDiscarding J2 maximizes hand flexibility and aligns with potential low-risk patterns like All Simples and All Chows, while avoiding blocking possible sequences.  \n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
